Loop: `while (curr < end)` (56) + `val = *curr;` (57) — index `curr` derived from `pptr`, bounded by `end`; termination via `curr++` (60). `while (1)` (55) exits `break` at 66 after `offset >= size` (64-66). End `for (i = 0; i < len; i++)` (112) with `len = min(...)` (82) — guard `i < len`; writes `n |= mask` (113). No unguarded access.

Evidence anchoring: source `offset` / sink `*curr` quoted at 23-26 and 56-57; guard `curr < end` applies to derived pointer `curr`; no mismatch between guard object and sink object. No auth/format sink observed.

Verdict is conservative false — both source and sink visible with guard applied; missing derived-pointer quote at every individual write reduces confidence but does not create vulnerability.

